dhamma tells a dog's story but behind  the scenes things allegedly got ugly in  a different way when you craft a story  about one of the world's most depraved  serial killers you can probably expect  some backlash Netflix is getting that  backlash from several directions over  their latest Based on a True Crime Story  the ever so slightly confusingly titled  Dharma monster the Jeffrey Dahmer story  starring Evan Peters as the infamous  Jeffrey Dahmer this streaming series  looks at both dharma's childhood and his  victims the details behind the killings  are sordid and stomach churning which is  why the story of the crimes have been  told and retold over and over again in  books movies and now this limited series  currently holding around a 53 critic  score and an 84 audience score on Rotten  Tomatoes Dharma is proving to be  divisive with audiences but the  production of the series was also a  struggle for some of the people involved  here's why despite the lukewarm critical  response to the show the popularity of  Netflix's Dharma series is off the  charts already the show is set a  staggering record by being the most  watched program in 60 countries and  netting around  196.2 million viewed hours according to  variety the show also generated  headlines after some viewers expressed  misgivings with Netflix tagging the  streaming show with an lgbtq tag some  viewers perceive this tag as being more  appropriate for more light-hearted  inclusive content and not shows  involving serial killers the backlash  was loud enough that Netflix ended up  removing the tag this isn't the only  negative headline to come dharma's way  although The Killers crime spree took  place more than 30 years ago some of  dharma's victims have family members who  are very much Alive Rita Isbell who was  the sister of 19 year old victim Errol  Lindsay had her statement from Jeffrey  Dahmer's trial recreated in Netflix's  show which didn't exactly sit well with  her in an essay published by Insider  Isabel shared her thoughts about the  Netflix series and the renewed notoriety  brought her a brother and her brother's  killer after watching some of the series  she says that the content bothered her  especially the moment where her impact  statement was recreated verbatim under  her real name she said I was never  contacted about the show I feel like  Netflix should have asked if we mind or  how we felt about making it they didn't  ask me anything they just did whatever  your name is Satan  I'm bad Lindsay said the recreation made  her feel like she was living the moment  all over again and the fact that she and  other victims families appear to have  got nothing out of the arrangements at  poorly with her she said I'm not money  hungry and that's what this show is  about Netflix trying to get paid it's  sad that they're just making money off  of this tragedy that's just greed on  sets not everyone was happy with the  Dharma series either one of their  production assistants on Dharma said it  was one of the worst sets they have ever  worked on according to the LA Times  production assistant Kim allsup wrote in  a now private tweet I worked on this  project and I was one of two black  people on the crew and they kept calling  me her name we both had braids she was  dark skinned and five foot ten I'm five  foot five working on this took  everything I had as I was treated  horribly in an interview at the LA Times  allsup elaborated that she hadn't  watched the series saying I just feel  like it's going to bring back too many  memories of working on it I don't want  to have these PTSD types of situations  the trailer itself gave me PTSD which is  why I ended up writing that tweet and I  didn't think that anybody was going to  read all sub also lamented that Dharma  was quote one of the worst shows that  I've ever worked on and alleged that  there were no mental health coordinators  available on set a Netflix spokesperson  told the LA Times that all crew are  provided access to free Health and  Wellness Resources including therapists  regardless it seems as if controversy  has followed this new show as almost  every step of the process even in some  ways you wouldn't expect it to turn up
 

